Polars
PHP




integer types
int (UInt64 values beyond PHP_INT_MAX become float)


Float32, Float64
float


Boolean
bool


String, Categorical
string


Date, Datetime
DateTimeImmutable (naive values in UTC, zoned values in their zone)


Time
string, "HH:MM:SS.ffffff"


Duration
int in the column’s time unit


Decimal
string


List, Array
list


Struct
associative array



From PHP, each column gets one inferred type. Integers widen to floats, nulls fit any type, DateTimeInterface values become naive Datetime(us) on their wall-clock time (the zone is not kept; use dt()-&gt;replaceTimeZone() to attach one), lists become List, and associative arrays become Struct. Any other mix raises SchemaError; pass a schema to set types.

Errors
Polars errors are thrown as subclasses of Phpolars\PolarsError, named after the py-polars exceptions: ColumnNotFoundError, ComputeError, DuplicateError, InvalidOperationError, NoDataError, OutOfBoundsError, SchemaError, SchemaFieldNotFoundError, ShapeError, and StructFieldNotFoundError, all in Phpolars\Exception. Invalid arguments raise PHP’s ValueError.
use Phpolars\Exception\{ColumnNotFoundError, SchemaError};

$df = new DataFrame(['a' =&gt; [1, 2]]);

try {
    $df-&gt;select('b');
} catch (ColumnNotFoundError $e) {
    echo get_class($e), ': ', strtok($e-&gt;getMessage(), "\n"), "\n";
}
try {
    new DataFrame(['a' =&gt; [1, 'two']]);
} catch (SchemaError $e) {
    echo get_class($e), ': ', $e-&gt;getMessage(), "\n";
}
echo $e instanceof Phpolars\PolarsError ? "both extend Phpolars\\PolarsError\n" : '';
Phpolars\Exception\ColumnNotFoundError: not found: unable to find column "b"; valid columns: ["a"]
Phpolars\Exception\SchemaError: column 'a' mixes incompatible types; pass a dtype or cast first
both extend Phpolars\PolarsError

Creating frames
$df = new DataFrame(['a' =&gt; [1, 2], 'b' =&gt; ['x', 'y']]);          // columns
$df = new DataFrame([['a' =&gt; 1, 'b' =&gt; 'x'], ['a' =&gt; 2, 'b' =&gt; 'y']]);  // rows
$df = DataFrame::fromRows([[1, 'x'], [2, 'y']], schema: ['a' =&gt; 'Int32', 'b' =&gt; 'String']);
$df = new DataFrame(['a' =&gt; new Series('a', [1, 2])]);
$df = read_csv('data.csv');
$lf = $df-&gt;lazy();      // or scan_csv(), scan_parquet(), ...
A schema argument names columns and sets their types.

Iterating over groups
A GroupBy works with foreach, as py-polars’ does. The key is a list of the group’s key values, and the value is the group’s rows as a DataFrame:
foreach ($sales-&gt;groupBy('store', maintainOrder: true) as $key =&gt; $rows) {
    echo $key[0], ': ', $rows-&gt;height(), "\n";
}

Imports
Classes live in Phpolars and functions are namespaced, so import them:
use Phpolars\{DataFrame, Series};
use function Phpolars\{col, lit, when, read_csv};

Variadic arguments and **named
Where py-polars takes *exprs, the method is variadic. An associative array stands in for **named_exprs:
$df-&gt;select('a', col('b')-&gt;mul(2), ['c' =&gt; col('x')-&gt;sum()]);
$df-&gt;groupBy('g')-&gt;agg(col('x')-&gt;mean(), ['n' =&gt; len()]);
PHP does not allow parameters after a variadic one. Methods that need both take a single argument that accepts a name, an Expr, or a list:
$df-&gt;groupBy(['store', 'product'], maintainOrder: true);
col('x')-&gt;sum()-&gt;over(['g', 'h'], orderBy: 'day');
$df-&gt;drop('a', 'b');
